  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/84cd401cd3457a7c9a9f2493f5854ecfb101edd8</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/84cd401cd3457a7c9a9f2493f5854ecfb101edd8"/>
    <title>
        fix(standardcompute): drop $0 cost from the router model (#10100)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-10-18T01:36:22Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76407537?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>henrikdukefoss</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/henrikdukefoss</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix(standardcompute): drop $0 cost from the router model (#10100)

Standard Compute is sold as monthly plans with a USD compute budget that is
metered at the routed model&amp;#39;s cost, so the router id has no single per-token
price and is not free. Declaring cost 0/0 made consumers list it as $0.00.
Omit [cost] like other auto-routers whose price depends on the routed model
(openrouter/auto, pioneer/auto), and document prompt-caching support in the
model comment.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
